IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-periods`

-- ccc31-forms-custody.l4 -- Forms 24, 25, 26, 27, 30, 35, 39, 49 and 50 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46:
-- the warrants and orders by which a person is taken to, kept in, and released from custody, and the one record (Form 35) whose
-- text carries a default term. Layer 1: the law as the Forms state it, from the text alone, from no one's point of view.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- How to read a result (the rule of 2026-10-29, and NOTES.md): every decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN.
-- JUST TRUE: the Form's words reach the case. JUST FALSE: the Form says no in its own words (an "unless" once met, an "until" once
-- reached, an "if" that fails, a period that has run). NOTHING: not covered (the Form's premise ("Whereas ... This is therefore") is not
-- made out, a seam answer is not JUST TRUE, or the Form is silent). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every Form that commands a person is encoded twice: a decision function (asserted in ccc31-tests-custody.l4) and a regulative rule
-- (run with #TRACE there; the stable binary cannot assert a trace). The keeper's custody "until ..." has no deadline in the text, so
-- it is a decision function (the "until" bar of the ruling of 2026-11-05), and the regulative rule holds the keeper to it with SHANT.
-- Seam inputs, named as PLAN.md section 4 names them: `s 2 peace officer: ...` and `s 2 prison: ...` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, from ccc-definitions).
-- Dates are `Date day month year`. A period is a `Length of time` counted by ccc31-forms-periods.

§ `Form 24 (Section 550) -- Warrant of Committal of Witness for Failure to Enter into Recognizance`

-- src:18464 | FORM 24 (Section 550) Warrant of Committal of Witness for Failure to Enter into Recognizance
-- src:18465 | Canada,
-- src:18466 | Province of ,
-- src:18467 | (territorial division).
-- src:18468 | To the peace officers in the (territorial division) and to the keeper of the (prison) at :
-- src:18469 | Whereas A.B., in this warrant called the accused, was committed for trial on a charge that (state offence as in the information);
-- src:18470 | And whereas E.F., in this warrant called the witness, having appeared as a witness on the preliminary inquiry into the charge, and being required to enter into a recognizance to appear as a witness on the trial of the accused on the charge, has (failed or refused) to do so;
-- src:18471 | This is therefore to direct you, in Her Majesty’s name, to arrest, if necessary, and take and safely convey the witness to the (prison) at and there deliver them to the keeper of it, together with the following precept:
-- src:18472 | You, the keeper, are directed to receive the witness into your custody in the prison and keep them there safely until the trial of the accused on the charge, unless before that time the witness enters into the recognizance.
-- src:18473 | Dated (date), at (place).
-- src:18474 | (Signature of justice or clerk of the court)
@ref Form 24 (Section 550) (src:18464-18474)
DECLARE `form 24 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 24 arrest if necessary, take and convey the witness to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    `form 24 receive the witness into custody in the prison`
    `form 24 release the witness` HAS `form 24 the witness has entered into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The direction to the peace officers. Its grounds are the two recitals: the premise of "This is therefore to direct you".
@ref Form 24 (Section 550) (src:18468-18471)
GIVEN `the accused was committed for trial on the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness appeared as a witness on the preliminary inquiry into the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness was required to enter into a recognizance to appear as a witness on the trial of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness has failed or refused to enter into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the accused was committed for trial on the charge`
                AND `the witness appeared as a witness on the preliminary inquiry into the charge`
                AND `the witness was required to enter into a recognizance to appear as a witness on the trial of the accused`
                AND `the witness has failed or refused to enter into the recognizance`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is therefore to direct you": the direction rests on the recitals and the Form does not say what follows when one is not made out
        IF NOT (`s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the peace officers in the (territorial division)": the direction is addressed to peace officers, whose definition (s 2) is an input
        IF NOT (`s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "convey the witness to the (prison)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The keeper's precept: keep the witness safely until the trial, unless before then the witness enters into the recognizance.
-- Ruled 2026-11-05 (the "until" bar): JUST TRUE before the end event, JUST FALSE after; never "the witness has been released".
@ref Form 24 (Section 550) (src:18472)
GIVEN `the witness has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial of the accused on the charge has taken place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before the trial the witness has entered into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 24 the keeper is directed to keep the witness in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the witness has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "receive the witness into your custody": the precept to keep follows the receiving
        IF `before the trial the witness has entered into the recognizance`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless before that time the witness enters into the recognizance"
        IF `the trial of the accused on the charge has taken place`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "keep them there safely until the trial of the accused on the charge"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The two duties as regulative rules. No time is stated, so no WITHIN. The keeper SHANT release the witness (the "keep ... safely");
-- a release after the witness has entered into the recognizance is not a violation (the guard carries the "unless").
@ref Form 24 (Section 550) (src:18471-18472)
`form 24 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `form 24 arrest if necessary, take and convey the witness to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
        MUST `form 24 receive the witness into custody in the prison`
        HENCE (
            PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
            SHANT `form 24 release the witness` entered PROVIDED NOT entered
            LEST BREACH BY `the keeper of a prison` BECAUSE "the keeper released the witness before the trial although the witness had not entered into the recognizance"
        )
    )

§ `Form 25 (Section 708) -- Warrant of Committal for Contempt`

-- src:18476 | FORM 25 (Section 708) Warrant of Committal for Contempt
-- src:18477 | Canada,
-- src:18478 | Province of ,
-- src:18479 | (territorial division).
-- src:18480 | To the peace officers in the (territorial division) and to the keeper of the (prison) at (place):
-- src:18481 | Because E.F. of , in this warrant called the defaulter, was on (date) , at (place), convicted before for contempt because the defaulter did not attend before to give evidence on the trial of a charge that (state offence as in the information) against A.B. of , although (duly subpoenaed or bound by recognizance to appear and give evidence in that regard, as the case may be) and did not show any sufficient excuse for the default;
-- src:18482 | And because, following the conviction it was ordered that the defaulter (set out the punishment imposed);
-- src:18483 | And because the defaulter has not paid the amounts ordered to be paid; (delete if not applicable)
-- src:18484 | Therefore, you are ordered, in Her Majesty’s name, to arrest, if necessary, and take the defaulter and convey them safely to the prison at and there deliver them to its keeper, together with the following order:
-- src:18485 | You, the keeper, are ordered to receive the defaulter into your custody in this prison and keep them safely there* and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant.
-- src:18486 | (a) for the term of ;
-- src:18487 | (b) for the term of , unless the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter to the prison are sooner paid;
-- src:18488 | (c) for the term of and for the term of (if consecutive so state) unless the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter to the prison are sooner paid.
-- src:18489 | Dated (date), at (place).
-- src:18490 | (Signature of judge, provincial court judge, justice or clerk of the court)
-- src:18491 | (Seal, if required)
@ref Form 25 (Section 708) (src:18476-18491)
DECLARE `form 25 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 25 arrest if necessary, take and convey the defaulter to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    `form 25 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison`
    `form 25 release the defaulter` HAS `form 25 the sums and the costs and charges have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The order to the peace officers. Its grounds are the three recitals (the third "delete if not applicable").
@ref Form 25 (Section 708) (src:18480-18484)
GIVEN `the defaulter was convicted for contempt because they did not attend to give evidence on the trial of a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defaulter was duly subpoenaed or bound by recognizance to appear and give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defaulter did not show any sufficient excuse for the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a punishment was ordered following the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `amounts were ordered to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defaulter has not paid the amounts ordered to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the defaulter was convicted for contempt because they did not attend to give evidence on the trial of a charge`
                AND `the defaulter was duly subpoenaed or bound by recognizance to appear and give evidence`
                AND `the defaulter did not show any sufficient excuse for the default`
                AND `a punishment was ordered following the conviction`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Therefore, you are ordered": the order rests on the recitals "Because ... And because"
        IF `amounts were ordered to be paid` AND NOT `the defaulter has not paid the amounts ordered to be paid`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "And because the defaulter has not paid the amounts ordered to be paid; (delete if not applicable)": the recital stands only where amounts were ordered
        IF NOT (`s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the peace officers in the (territorial division)"
        IF NOT (`s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "convey them safely to the prison"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The order's three alternatives (the asterisk after "there" has no footnote in this text; NOTES.md finding).
DECLARE `form 25 the order as to the term` IS ONE OF
    `form 25 (a) for the term of`
    `form 25 (b) for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid`
    `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid`

-- The keeper's order: keep the defaulter safely for the term, with (b) and (c) "unless ... sooner paid" (the "until" bar).
-- Fork F1 ("unless" once met): payment before the date asked about is JUST FALSE for (b). Fork F2 ((c)): the "unless" is read to reach
-- the second term, the default term, only; if it were read to reach both, payment while the first term runs would end the custody.
-- The text does not choose: that case is NOTHING.
-- The date asked about is the day on which the question is put; `the day the defaulter was received into custody` is day 1 of the terms
-- (ccc31-forms-periods: the period begins on the day named).
@ref Form 25 (Section 708) (src:18485-18488)
GIVEN order IS A `form 25 the order as to the term`
      `the day the defaulter was received into custody` IS A DATE
      `the first term` IS A `Length of time`
      `the second term` IS A `Length of time`
      `the second term is stated to be consecutive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid before the date asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `form 25 (a) for the term of` THEN
        IF `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the date asked about` `the day the defaulter was received into custody` `the first term`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) for the term of ;"
    WHEN `form 25 (b) for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid before the date asked about`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter to the prison are sooner paid"
            IF NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the date asked about` `the day the defaulter was received into custody` `the first term`)
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) for the term of"
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the end of the two terms`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) for the term of and for the term of"
            IF `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid before the date asked about` AND `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the end of the first term`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter to the prison are sooner paid"
            IF `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid before the date asked about`
                THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the sums ... are sooner paid" follows both terms and the text does not say whether payment ends the first term (fork F2)
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the end of the first term` MEANS
            `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` `the day the defaulter was received into custody` `the first term`
        `the end of the two terms` MEANS
            IF `the second term is stated to be consecutive`
            THEN `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` `the end of the first term` `the second term`
            ELSE `the later of the two ends`
        `the later of the two ends` MEANS
            IF `the end of the first term` AT LEAST (`forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` `the day the defaulter was received into custody` `the second term`)
            THEN `the end of the first term`
            ELSE `forms 24-54 the first day after a period that begins on a day` `the day the defaulter was received into custody` `the second term`

-- "and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant": the keeper who keeps the defaulter as the order directs is protected by the warrant.
@ref Form 25 (Section 708) (src:18485)
GIVEN `the keeper keeps the defaulter in custody as the order directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 25 this is a sufficient warrant for the keeper` MEANS
    IF `the keeper keeps the defaulter in custody as the order directs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant": the warrant is sufficient "for so doing", and the Form is silent on keeping otherwise

@ref Form 25 (Section 708) (src:18484-18488)
`form 25 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `form 25 arrest if necessary, take and convey the defaulter to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
        MUST `form 25 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    )

§ `Form 26 (Section 827) -- Warrant of Committal in Default of Payment of Costs of an Appeal`

-- src:18493 | FORM 26 (Section 827) Warrant of Committal in Default of Payment of Costs of an Appeal
-- src:18494 | Canada,
-- src:18495 | Province of ,
-- src:18496 | (territorial division).
-- src:18497 | To the peace officers of (territorial division) and to the keeper of the (prison) at :
-- src:18498 | Whereas it appears that on the hearing of an appeal before the (set out court) it was adjudged that A.B., of , hereinafter called the defaulter, should pay to the Clerk of the Court the sum of dollars in respect of costs;
-- src:18499 | And Whereas the Clerk of the Court has certified that the defaulter has not paid the sum within the time limited therefor;
-- src:18500 | I do hereby command you, the said peace officers, in Her Majesty’s name, to take the defaulter and safely convey him to the (prison) at and deliver him to the keeper thereof, together with the following precept:
-- src:18501 | I do hereby command you, the said keeper, to receive the defaulter into your custody in the said prison and imprison him for the term of , unless the said sum and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter to the said prison are sooner paid, and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant.
-- src:18502 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18503 | A Justice of the Peace in and for
@ref Form 26 (Section 827) (src:18493-18503)
DECLARE `form 26 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 26 take the defaulter and convey them to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    `form 26 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison`

@ref Form 26 (Section 827) (src:18497-18500)
GIVEN `on the hearing of an appeal it was adjudged that the defaulter should pay costs to the Clerk of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Clerk of the Court has certified that the defaulter has not paid the sum within the time limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 26 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the defaulter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `on the hearing of an appeal it was adjudged that the defaulter should pay costs to the Clerk of the Court`
                AND `the Clerk of the Court has certified that the defaulter has not paid the sum within the time limited`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "I do hereby command you": the command rests on the two recitals "Whereas ... And Whereas"
        IF NOT (`s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the peace officers of (territorial division)"
        IF NOT (`s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "safely convey him to the (prison)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The keeper's command: imprison the defaulter for the term, unless the sum and the costs and charges are sooner paid. The sum, and the
-- costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter, must ALL be paid to end the custody (fork F1: an "unless" once met).
@ref Form 26 (Section 827) (src:18501)
GIVEN `the defaulter has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the defaulter was received into custody` IS A DATE
      term IS A `Length of time`
      `the sum has been paid before the date asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter have been paid before the date asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the defaulter has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "receive the defaulter into your custody in the said prison and imprison him": the command to imprison follows the receiving
        IF `the sum has been paid before the date asked about` AND `the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter have been paid before the date asked about`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the said sum and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the defaulter to the said prison are sooner paid"
        IF NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the date asked about` `the day the defaulter was received into custody` term)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "imprison him for the term of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Form 26 (Section 827) (src:18501)
GIVEN `the keeper keeps the defaulter in custody as the warrant commands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 26 this is a sufficient warrant for the keeper` MEANS
    IF `the keeper keeps the defaulter in custody as the warrant commands`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and for so doing this is a sufficient warrant": the warrant is sufficient "for so doing"

@ref Form 26 (Section 827) (src:18500-18501)
`form 26 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `form 26 take the defaulter and convey them to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
        MUST `form 26 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    )

§ `Form 27 (Section 773) -- Warrant of Committal on Forfeiture of Amounts`

-- src:18505 | FORM 27 (Section 773) Warrant of Committal on Forfeiture of Amounts
-- src:18506 | Canada,
-- src:18507 | Province of ,
-- src:18508 | (territorial division).
-- src:18509 | To the sheriff of (territorial division) and to the keeper of the (prison) at (place).
-- src:18510 | This warrant of committal is issued for the arrest of (name of person or persons), referred to in this warrant as the defaulter or defaulters, as the case may be.
-- src:18511 | You are ordered to arrest the defaulter or defaulters and convey them safely to the (prison) at , and deliver them to its keeper, with the following order:
-- src:18512 | You, the keeper, are ordered to receive the defaulter or defaulters into your custody in this prison and keep them safely there for a period of or until satisfaction is made of a judgment debt of , due to Her Majesty the Queen in respect of the forfeiture of an amount set out in (an undertaking entered into or a release order issued or a recognizance entered into) on (date).
-- src:18513 | Dated (date), at (place).
-- src:18514 | (Signature of judge of the court or clerk of the court)
-- src:18515 | (Name of judge who has issued this warrant of committal)
-- src:18516 | (Seal, if required)
@ref Form 27 (Section 773) (src:18505-18516)
DECLARE `form 27 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 27 arrest the defaulter and convey them to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    `form 27 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison`

-- The warrant is addressed to the sheriff, who is a peace officer under paragraph (a) of the definition in s 2 (the core's `Party` has
-- no sheriff: NEEDS-CORE.md). The order to arrest rests on the warrant being issued for the defaulter named.
@ref Form 27 (Section 773) (src:18509-18511)
GIVEN `the warrant was issued for the arrest of the defaulter named in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 27 the sheriff is ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the warrant was issued for the arrest of the defaulter named in it`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This warrant of committal is issued for the arrest of (name of person or persons)"
        IF NOT (`s 2 prison: the place named is a prison` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "convey them safely to the (prison)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The keeper's order: keep the defaulter "for a period of ___ or until satisfaction is made of a judgment debt". Fork F3: read as ending at
-- the EARLIER of the end of the period and the satisfaction of the debt. The other reading takes them as two alternatives of which the
-- completer chooses one; it gives the same answer when the Form is completed with one of them (the other input is then ignored by the caller).
@ref Form 27 (Section 773) (src:18512)
GIVEN `the defaulter has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt is due to Her Majesty in respect of the forfeiture of an amount set out in an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the defaulter was received into custody` IS A DATE
      period IS A `Length of time`
      `satisfaction has been made of the judgment debt before the date asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 27 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the defaulter has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "receive the defaulter or defaulters into your custody in this prison and keep them safely there"
        IF NOT `the debt is due to Her Majesty in respect of the forfeiture of an amount set out in an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judgment debt of , due to Her Majesty the Queen in respect of the forfeiture of an amount set out in"
        IF `satisfaction has been made of the judgment debt before the date asked about`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until satisfaction is made of a judgment debt"
        IF NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the date asked about` `the day the defaulter was received into custody` period)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Form 27 (Section 773) (src:18511-18512)
`form 27 the duties of the sheriff and the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `form 27 arrest the defaulter and convey them to the prison and deliver them to the keeper`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
        MUST `form 27 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    )

§ `Form 30 (Section 537) -- Order for Accused to Be Brought Before Justice Prior to Expiration of Period of Remand`

-- src:18546 | FORM 30 (Section 537) Order for Accused to Be Brought Before Justice Prior to Expiration of Period of Remand
-- src:18547 | Canada,
-- src:18548 | Province of ,
-- src:18549 | (territorial division).
-- src:18550 | To the keeper of the (prison) at :
-- src:18551 | Whereas by warrant dated (date), A.B., in this order called the accused, was committed to your custody and you were required to keep them safely until the (date), and then to have them before me or any other justice (or if the signatory is not the justice, any justice) at (place) at (hour) to answer to the charge against the accused and to be dealt with according to law unless you should be ordered otherwise before that time;
-- src:18552 | Now, therefore, you are directed to have the accused before at (place) at (hour) to answer to the charge against them and so they may be dealt with according to law.
-- src:18553 | Dated (date), at (place).
-- src:18554 | (Signature of justice or clerk of the court)
@ref Form 30 (Section 537) (src:18546-18554)
DECLARE `form 30 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 30 have the accused before the justice at the place and hour`

-- The direction rests on the recital: the keeper holds the accused under a warrant requiring the keeper to keep them until a date and then
-- have them before a justice, "unless you should be ordered otherwise before that time", and this order is made before that time.
@ref Form 30 (Section 537) (src:18551-18552)
GIVEN `by warrant the accused was committed to the keeper's custody for a period of remand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this order is made before the period of remand expires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 30 the keeper is directed to have the accused before the justice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `by warrant the accused was committed to the keeper's custody for a period of remand`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Whereas by warrant dated (date), A.B., in this order called the accused, was committed to your custody"
        IF NOT `this order is made before the period of remand expires`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless you should be ordered otherwise before that time": the order is the one made "Prior to Expiration of Period of Remand", and the Form is silent after it
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the keeper must have the accused before the justice at the hour stated. The deadline is the number of
-- hours from the order to the hour stated (the unit of this clock is hours; the text names an hour, not a period).
@ref Form 30 (Section 537) (src:18552)
GIVEN `the hours from the order to the hour stated` IS A NUMBER
`form 30 the duty of the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
    MUST `form 30 have the accused before the justice at the place and hour`
    WITHIN `the hours from the order to the hour stated`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the keeper of a prison` BECAUSE "the keeper did not have the accused before the justice at the place and hour stated"

§ `Form 35 (Sections 570 and 806) -- Conviction`

-- src:18752 | FORM 35 (Sections 570 and 806) Conviction
-- src:18753 | Canada,
-- src:18754 | Province of ,
-- src:18755 | (territorial division).
-- src:18756 | Be it remembered that on the day of at , A.B., (date of birth) hereinafter called the accused, was tried under Part (XIX or XXVII) of the Criminal Code on the charge that (state fully the offence of which accused was convicted), was convicted of the said offence and the following punishment was imposed on him, namely,*
-- src:18757 | (a) that the said accused be imprisoned in the (prison) at for the term of ;
-- src:18758 | (b) that the said accused forfeit and pay the sum of dollars to be applied according to law and also pay to the sum of dollars in respect of costs and in default of payment of the said sums forthwith (or within a time fixed, if any), to be imprisoned in the (prison) at for the term of unless the said sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the accused to the said prison are sooner paid;
-- src:18759 | (c) that the said accused be imprisoned in the (prison) at for the term of and in addition forfeit and pay the sum of dollars to be applied according to law and also pay to the sum of dollars in respect of costs and in default of payment of the said sums forthwith (or within a time fixed, if any), to be imprisoned in the (prison) at for the term of (if sentence to be consecutive, state accordingly) unless the said sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the accused to the said prison are sooner paid.
-- src:18760 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18761 | Clerk of the Court, Justice or Provincial Court Judge
-- src:18762 | (Seal, if required)
@ref Form 35 (Sections 570 and 806) (src:18752-18762)
DECLARE `form 35 the punishment imposed` IS ONE OF
    `form 35 (a) imprisonment for the term of`
    `form 35 (b) a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default`
    `form 35 (c) imprisonment and, in addition, a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default`

-- The default term of (b) and (c): "in default of payment of the said sums forthwith (or within a time fixed, if any), to be imprisoned in
-- the prison for the term of ___ unless the said sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the accused to the said
-- prison are sooner paid". It reaches (c)'s default term only (the first term of (c) is the imprisonment "in addition"); fork F1.
@ref Form 35 (Sections 570 and 806) (src:18758-18759)
GIVEN punishment IS A `form 35 the punishment imposed`
      `the sums were not paid forthwith or within the time fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the accused was received into custody in default` IS A DATE
      `the default term` IS A `Length of time`
      `the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the accused have been paid before the date asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF punishment EQUALS `form 35 (a) imprisonment for the term of`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) states imprisonment for a term and no default term
        IF NOT `the sums were not paid forthwith or within the time fixed`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in default of payment of the said sums forthwith (or within a time fixed, if any)"
        IF `the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the accused have been paid before the date asked about`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the said sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying the accused to the said prison are sooner paid"
        IF NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the date asked about` `the day the accused was received into custody in default` `the default term`)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to be imprisoned in the (prison) at for the term of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 39 (Sections 519 and 550) -- Order for Discharge of a Person in Custody`

-- src:18791 | FORM 39 (Sections 519 and 550) Order for Discharge of a Person in Custody
-- src:18792 | Canada,
-- src:18793 | Province of ,
-- src:18794 | (territorial division).
-- src:18795 | To the keeper of the (prison) at :
-- src:18796 | You are directed to release E.F., detained by you under a (warrant of committal or order) dated (date), if E.F. is detained by you for no other cause.
-- src:18797 | (Signature of judge, justice or clerk of the court)
-- src:18798 | (Seal, if required)
@ref Form 39 (Sections 519 and 550) (src:18791-18798)
DECLARE `form 39 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 39 release the person`

@ref Form 39 (Sections 519 and 550) (src:18795-18796)
GIVEN `the person is detained by the keeper under the warrant of committal or order the discharge names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is detained by the keeper for another cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 39 the keeper is directed to release the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is detained by the keeper under the warrant of committal or order the discharge names`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "release E.F., detained by you under a (warrant of committal or order) dated (date)"
        IF `the person is detained by the keeper for another cause`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if E.F. is detained by you for no other cause"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Form 39 (Sections 519 and 550) (src:18796)
`form 39 the duty of the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
    MUST `form 39 release the person`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Form 49 (Section 672.57) -- Warrant of Committal: Disposition of Detention`

-- src:18950 | FORM 49 (Section 672.57) Warrant of Committal
-- src:18952 | Disposition of Detention
-- src:18953 | Canada,
-- src:18954 | Province of
-- src:18955 | (territorial division)
-- src:18956 | To the peace officers in the said (territorial division) and to the keeper (administrator, warden) of the (prison, hospital or other appropriate place where the accused is detained).
-- src:18957 | This warrant is issued for the committal of A.B., of , (occupation), hereinafter called the accused.
-- src:18958 | Whereas the accused has been charged that (set out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused was charged);
-- src:18959 | And whereas the accused was found*
-- src:18960 | ☐ unfit to stand trial
-- src:18961 | ☐ not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder
-- src:18962 | This is, therefore, to command you, in Her Majesty’s name, to take the accused in custody and convey the accused safely to the (prison, hospital or other appropriate place) at , and there deliver the accused to the keeper (administrator, warden) with the following precept:
-- src:18963 | You, the keeper (administrator, warden), are therefore directed to receive the accused in your custody in the (prison, hospital or other appropriate place) and to keep the accused safely there until the accused is delivered by due course of law.
-- src:18964 | The following are the conditions to which the accused shall be subject while in your (prison, hospital or other appropriate place):
-- src:18965 | The following are the powers regarding the restrictions (and the limits and conditions on those restrictions) on the liberty of the accused that are hereby delegated to you the said keeper (administrator, warden) of the said (prison, hospital or other appropriate place):
-- src:18966 | Dated (date), at (place).
-- src:18967 | (Signature of judge, provincial court judge, justice, clerk of the court or chairperson of the review board)
@ref Form 49 (Section 672.57) (src:18950-18967)
DECLARE `form 49 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 49 take the accused in custody and convey them to the place and deliver them to the keeper`
    `form 49 receive the accused into custody in the place`

-- The command to the peace officers rests on the charge and on the finding (unfit to stand trial, or not criminally responsible on account of
-- mental disorder: the two boxes, one to be ticked). The place is "(prison, hospital or other appropriate place)".
@ref Form 49 (Section 672.57) (src:18956-18962)
GIVEN `the accused has been charged with the offence the warrant sets out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was found unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place named is a prison, hospital or other appropriate place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 49 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the accused has been charged with the offence the warrant sets out`
                AND (`the accused was found unfit to stand trial` OR `the accused was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`))
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is, therefore, to command you": the command rests on the recitals "Whereas the accused has been charged ... And whereas the accused was found"
        IF NOT `the place named is a prison, hospital or other appropriate place`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "convey the accused safely to the (prison, hospital or other appropriate place)"
        IF NOT (`s 2 peace officer: the person addressed is a peace officer in the territorial division` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the peace officers in the said (territorial division)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The keeper's precept: keep the accused safely "until the accused is delivered by due course of law" (the "until" bar of 2026-11-05;
-- what counts as delivery by due course of law is an input).
@ref Form 49 (Section 672.57) (src:18963)
GIVEN `the accused has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been delivered by due course of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 49 the keeper is directed to keep the accused in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "receive the accused in your custody in the (prison, hospital or other appropriate place)"
        IF `the accused has been delivered by due course of law`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the accused is delivered by due course of law"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "The following are the conditions to which the accused shall be subject while in your (prison, hospital or other appropriate place)".
@ref Form 49 (Section 672.57) (src:18964)
GIVEN `the condition is one the warrant lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is in the keeper's prison, hospital or other place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 49 the accused is subject to the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the condition is one the warrant lists`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following are the conditions to which the accused shall be subject"
        IF NOT `the accused is in the keeper's prison, hospital or other place`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while in your (prison, hospital or other appropriate place)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "The following are the powers regarding the restrictions (and the limits and conditions on those restrictions) on the liberty of the accused
-- that are hereby delegated to you the said keeper": a power the warrant delegates to the keeper.
@ref Form 49 (Section 672.57) (src:18965)
GIVEN `the power is one the warrant lists as delegated to the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 49 the keeper holds the delegated power` MEANS
    IF `the power is one the warrant lists as delegated to the keeper`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following are the powers ... that are hereby delegated to you": a power the warrant does not list is not covered

@ref Form 49 (Section 672.57) (src:18962-18963)
`form 49 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `form 49 take the accused in custody and convey them to the place and deliver them to the keeper`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
        MUST `form 49 receive the accused into custody in the place`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    )

§ `Form 50 (Subsection 672.7(2)) -- Warrant of Committal: Placement Decision`

-- src:18969 | FORM 50 (Subsection 672.7(2)) Warrant of Committal
-- src:18971 | Placement Decision
-- src:18972 | Canada,
-- src:18973 | Province of
-- src:18974 | (territorial division)
-- src:18975 | To the peace officers in the said (territorial division) and to the keeper (administrator, warden) of the (prison, hospital or other appropriate place where the accused is detained).
-- src:18976 | This warrant is issued for the committal of A.B., of , (occupation), hereinafter called the accused.
-- src:18977 | Whereas the accused has been charged that (set out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused was charged);
-- src:18978 | And whereas the accused was found*
-- src:18979 | ☐ unfit to stand trial
-- src:18980 | ☐ not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder
-- src:18981 | And whereas the Review Board has held a hearing and decided that the accused shall be detained in custody;
-- src:18982 | And whereas the accused is required to be detained in custody pursuant to a warrant of committal issued by (set out the name of the Judge, Clerk of the Court, Provincial Court Judge or Justice as well as the name of the court and territorial division), dated the day of , in respect of the offence that (set out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused was charged or convicted);
-- src:18983 | This is, therefore, to command you, in Her Majesty’s name, to*
-- src:18984 | ☐ execute the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms
-- src:18985 | ☐ execute the warrant of committal issued herewith by the Review Board
-- src:18986 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18987 | (Signature of chairperson of the Review Board)
@ref Form 50 (Subsection 672.7(2)) (src:18969-18987)
DECLARE `form 50 the warrant to execute` IS ONE OF
    `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms`
    `form 50 the warrant of committal issued herewith by the Review Board`

DECLARE `form 50 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 50 execute the warrant`

-- The command rests on the recitals (the charge, the finding, the Review Board's decision to detain, the court's earlier warrant). The
-- command is to do ONE of two things, whichever box is ticked: the question names the warrant asked about and the box that was ticked.
@ref Form 50 (Subsection 672.7(2)) (src:18975-18985)
GIVEN `the accused has been charged with the offence the warrant sets out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was found unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board has held a hearing and decided that the accused shall be detained in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is required to be detained in custody pursuant to a warrant of committal issued by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the box ticked` IS A `form 50 the warrant to execute`
      `the warrant asked about` IS A `form 50 the warrant to execute`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the accused has been charged with the offence the warrant sets out`
                AND `the accused was found unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`
                AND `the Review Board has held a hearing and decided that the accused shall be detained in custody`
                AND `the accused is required to be detained in custody pursuant to a warrant of committal issued by a court`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is, therefore, to command you": the command rests on the four recitals
        IF `the box ticked` EQUALS `the warrant asked about`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to* ... execute the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms ... execute the warrant of committal issued herewith by the Review Board": two alternatives, one ticked; the Form says nothing of the one not ticked

@ref Form 50 (Subsection 672.7(2)) (src:18983-18985)
`form 50 the duty of the keeper` MEANS
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
    MUST `form 50 execute the warrant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
